{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1004222-how-would-your-character-rob-a-bank-pull-off-a-jewel-art-other-classic-heists","id":1004222,"title":"How would your character rob a bank/pull off a jewel/art/ other classic heists?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-16T20:31:29-08:00","id":1004222,"title":"How would your character rob a bank/pull off a jewel/art/ other classic heists?","content":"Exactly what it sounds like, how would your PCs (or NPCs for the STs out there) pull off one of the classic heist types?<br /> <br /> I have an old Ventrue PC I wrote up but never played who would probably do the bank job using the 15 minutes or less method (meaning dominate a pizza guy and strap a bomb to him and make him rob the bank for him), said Ventrue was supposed to be a bit of a dip shit who was embraced as a result of being mistaken for the guy his sire really wanted to embrace, so I gladly would have accepted a dramatic failure on making that plan.<br /> <br /> As for a Jewel or art heist, my movie producer werewolf Joshua Planter would use have his pack's totem, a spirit representing Hollywood and the glamour of the movie industry, use it's 4 dot Influence over tropes to deliberately invoke heist movie tropes to make sure his pack got away with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T21:00:48-08:00","id":1004231,"title":"","content":"In the last game I ran the vampires were all thieves to some extent, and would just use Obfuscate and other abilities to gain access to rooms. In one case they used celerity upon breaking through a window to make it to the stairwell across the room before the security gate shut and blocked it off.<br /> <br /> My werewolf would simply tell alarms or security devices to shut off. He never got Shutdown but that would have made things a lot easier. He broke into many places but only managed a few stealth break-ins, as he had a propensity towards eating people and as the game developed the people guarding things became less reputable and more disposable. Not quite a standard 'heist' but another player whose character was physically stronger basically broke through doors and gates for us when we needed to get through.<br /> <br /> Oh in another game of Changeling my character eventually picked up the Contracts of Separation, and the third dot allowed him to open doors, the fifth dot to phase through things. He robbed a jewelry store at one point, though it wasn't for anything special. I think one piece ended up being unique, it had a name on it or something.<br /> <br /> Currently I'm running mage, where I imagine the players would have little problems performing heists if they wanted. I was going to have some more magical-oriented ones, I was able to encourage the Mystagoge into being a reclaimant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-17-2016, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T03:06:45-08:00","id":1004316,"title":"","content":"Anyone with the Space Arcanum at three dots can basically break into almost anywhere as long as there's no supernatural security measures. My Space 4 Mastigos would do it blindfolded and with one hand tied behind his back.<br /> Park your car outside the place you want to rob. Cast The Outward and Inward Eye to see everything inside the place. Cast Co-Location on your location and on your target's location. Take the target while still sitting in the car. Drive off.<br /> You'd only idle for about ten seconds. If you have a driver they could just slow down outside the target to give you enough time to locate the object and cast Co-Location before driving off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T18:09:28-08:00","id":1004731,"title":"","content":"Bind a spirit with Shadow Gateway into opening the vaults from within the Hisil, grab all that you want, exit in the same fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}